External proof-of-concept smoke data
------------------------------------

The optional six-sample external smoke set is:

Henzelin, Kenan; Risse, Lucas; Patiny, Luc (2025), "Proof-of-Concept
Dataset of Chemical Structures with NMR, IR and MS Spectra", Zenodo,
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16881130, CC0-1.0.

It is used only as a proof-of-concept interoperability smoke set. Six samples
are not sufficient for a headline model-accuracy or generalization claim.

NMRexp human-reviewed data
--------------------------

The optional human-reviewed peak-annotation pool is:

Wang, Jun-Jie; Zhu, Rong (2025), "NMRexp: A database of 3.37 million
experimental NMR spectra", Zenodo,
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17296666, CC BY 4.0.

License:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Associated publication:
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-06245-5

ChemApp selects only six fixed *_checked.csv files. Derived records preserve
their source DOI and this attribution. See THIRD_PARTY_DATA.md and
docs/independent-nmr-sources-v1.json.

NMR-Solver manually curated paired-spectrum benchmark
-----------------------------------------------------

The optional v4 research benchmark is:

Jin, Yongqi et al. (2025), "NMR-Solver: Automated Molecular Structure
Elucidation via Large-Scale Spectra Matching and Physics-Guided Fragment
Optimization", Zenodo,
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16952024, CC BY 4.0.

License:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Associated publication:
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-71315-0

ChemApp reads only the fixed data/experiment/test.txt member. The upstream
collection is described as manually curated, but it has no per-row reviewer,
review timestamp, or source-document mapping and is not represented as
ChemApp double-reviewed data. Derived redistributions must retain their
ATTRIBUTION.json. See THIRD_PARTY_DATA.md and
docs/nmrsolver-reviewed-source-v1.json.

